<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO ups Van Melle to buy.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO ups Van Melle to buy.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of March 7 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>    Van Melle	 Confectionery 153.00  ABN AMRO Hoare Govett</p>
<p>COMMENT: BUY (Hold). Full-year 1996 results last week were slightly below the management forecasts at the interim stage, with net profit rising 6 pct to DFl 51 million. Drop in share price of 11 pct was exaggerated. Strong underlying growth was overshadowed by higher advertising and promotion spending. Longer term potential of expansion in highly profitable existing markets -- the U.S. and in new Asian markets, where Van Melle is currently taking positions -- should secure superior growth.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS	 P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     5.98	24.7   15.6   2.10</p>
<p>    1997		  6.65	22.3   13.4   2.30</p>
<p>    1998		  7.45	19.9   11.9   2.60</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
